# Adopted from FastEMRIWaveforms' citation pattern (Phase 4, 2026-06-02).
# This file lists the canonical bibliography for LISAanalysistools and the
# papers users should cite when using the package. The
# `lisatools.utils.citations` module parses this file at runtime so each
# class can declare a `module_references()` list that gets rendered into
# a BibTeX string via `MyClass.citation()` or the `lisatools_citations`
# CLI.

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: LISAanalysistools
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the package itself and
  the references specific to the modules / classes you use (see each
  class's `module_references()` method and the documentation).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Michael
    family-names: Katz
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7605-5767'
    affiliation: NASA Marshall Space Flight Center
    email: mikekatz04@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/mikekatz04/LISAanalysistools'
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Tooling for LISA (Laser Interferometer Space Antenna) data analysis
  -- orbit definitions, sensitivity matrices, analysis containers,
  source-class waveform generators, the LISA global fit pipeline, and
  JAX / CUDA / CPU backends for response and TDI machinery.

# Module-specific references. Each entry's `key` is what classes pass
# into their `module_references()` list. Keep this list flat (no
# nesting); new references are appended.
references:
  - type: article
    key: GlobalFitKatz2024
    title: "Efficient global fit of the LISA data with the gravitational-wave source population"
    authors:
      - given-names: Michael L.
        family-names: Katz
    year: 2024
    note: Placeholder -- update with the canonical global-fit paper when published.
  - type: article
    key: WDMheterodyne
    title: "WDM-domain heterodyne template likelihoods for LISA"
    authors:
      - given-names: Michael L.
        family-names: Katz
    year: 2026
    note: Placeholder -- chunked-heterodyne paper reference; update when on arXiv.
